1. PROJECT OVERVIEW
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Go Deliver is a full-stack, enterprise-grade urban delivery and courier platform.
It provides instant customer delivery booking, multi-step courier quote requests,
real-time dispatch tracking by unique tracking codes, and an administrative control
panel for fleet dispatchers to manage requests, services, service coverage areas,
frequently asked questions (FAQs), multi-channel contact endpoints (WhatsApp,
Facebook, Telegram, Phone lines), and dispatcher administrative accounts.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. TECH STACK SPECIFICATION
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
A. Frontend:
   - Framework: React 18.2 with TypeScript (TSX)
   - Build Tool & Dev Server: Vite 5
   - Styling: Tailwind CSS with customized brand palette:
     * Brand Red: #E53935 / Hover: #D32F2F
     * Brand Dark: #0F1115 / Secondary: #171A21
     * Brand Light: #F8F9FA / Border: #E2E8F0
     * JetBrains Mono for tracking & numerical codes
     * Plus Jakarta Sans for UI typography
   - Routing: React Router DOM v6 (Client-side single-page app)
   - Icons: Lucide React (feather-style modern vector icons)
   - Maps: Leaflet & OpenStreetMap integration with custom courier dispatch markers
   - Validation: Custom strict numeric & phone sanitizers (blocks all non-digits)

B. Backend:
   - Runtime: Node.js (via tsx execution engine)
   - Web Server: Express 4.18
   - Security: Helmet (CSP configured for framed preview), CORS with credentials,
     and express-rate-limit protecting API endpoints
   - Authentication: HTTP-only cookies & Bearer JWT token verification
   - Password Hashing: Node.js crypto scrypt with unique salt per password
   - Database ORM: Prisma ORM (v5) with SQLite database (prisma/dev.db)
     Easily swappable to PostgreSQL / Cloud SQL via DATABASE_URL

C. Unified Server:
   - server.ts: Dual-mode single entry point running on port 3000.
     In development, acts as an API proxy forwarding client routes to Vite.
     In production, statically serves compiled frontend bundle with SPA fallback.

